<section class="solaris-section solaris-how-it-works" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="solaris-container">
    <div class="solaris-section-head">
      <p class="solaris-eyebrow">HOW IT WORKS</p>
      <h2 class="solaris-section-title">Understand what the tracker is actually doing.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="solaris-numbered-grid">
      <div class="solaris-numbered-block">
        <span class="solaris-number">01</span>
        <h3>Sun Position</h3>
        <p>The simulation calculates where the Sun is in the sky using latitude, time of day, and a simplified solar-position model.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="solaris-numbered-block">
        <span class="solaris-number">02</span>
        <h3>Incidence Angle</h3>
        <p>The system calculates the angle between incoming sunlight and the panel normal using vector geometry.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="solaris-numbered-block">
        <span class="solaris-number">03</span>
        <h3>Optimization</h3>
        <p>A Perturb &amp; Observe controller searches for an orientation that increases irradiance, step by step.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="solaris-numbered-block">
        <span class="solaris-number">04</span>
        <h3>Energy</h3>
        <p>The resulting irradiance is converted into simulated electrical power and integrated into energy over time.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
